      "content": "Dextromethorphan is a natural cough suppressant that works by blocking the brain's cough reflex, and it is safe to take with sertraline as long as you only take the standard adult dose of 15-30mg. You can mix it with a little honey to soothe your throat and then take it 30 minutes before bed to ensure you get those restful hours you need. Just remember to stick to the label dosage and avoid any other sleep aids, as your body will handle the combination perfectly fine.",
